id: pm-q2a7hr
title: Auto Release coverage depends on a /proc timing race in the SDK entrypoint sampler
description: "The August 3 production Auto Release run 30775382287 failed its exact 100% coverage gate because scripts/bench/sdk-entrypoint-costs.mjs line 93 is covered only when a sampled child exits between pid observation and /proc status read. Local full coverage happened to exercise the catch; hosted Node 24 did not, yielding 99.99% statements/lines. The sampler must expose deterministic bounded I/O injection so the failure path is proven without timing, process, or platform luck."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-03T01:01:22.454Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T01:29:18.294Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#aea157f022b12643c556d387"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The /proc read failure path is deterministically testable without relying on child-process timing; the focused test proves read failure returns undefined and mutations of that behavior fail coverage or assertions; full exact 100/100/100/100 coverage passes; the production Auto Release rerun passes without weakening thresholds or exclusions
parent: pm-u9d0
